{
  "name": "m30-30.3-understand-linux",
  "lesson": "30.1, 30.3",
  "title": "Lab 30.3, part 1: get the lab, see what each file is, one release file, look before you run, set up and check, then look at each idea of a security release gate on its own with explore.py (your own suite, one case, 20 trials of one case, confidence intervals, noise over 10 days, a score card, two releases compared, the naive gate over 10 days, the six gate rules, a gate log, the CI pipeline) and read one run line by line",
